Cloud Shell Terminal  vs Agent Studio
-------------------------------------

| Cloud Shell Terminal     | Agent Studio                        |
| ------------------------ | ----------------------------------- |
| 💻 Developer environment | 🎨 AI/Agent development workspace   |
| Mainly command line      | Mainly visual/UI                    |
| Write Python code        | Configure/design agents             |
| Run scripts              | Test/design AI applications         |
| Install packages         | Work with available AI capabilities |
| `python app.py`          | Build/test agent workflows          |
| `gcloud` commands        | Agent configuration                 |
| Full programming control | Easier agent experimentation        |
| Great for developers     | Great for prototyping agents        |


==========

Example: Build a customer-support AI
Using Cloud Shell
--------------

You might write:

---------
from google import genai

client = genai.Client(...)

response = client.models.generate_content(
    model="gemini-2.5-flash",
    contents="Answer this customer question..."
)

print(response.text)
-------------

You control the entire application.

You can add:

Python
 ↓
RAG
 ↓
FAISS
 ↓
Gemini
 ↓
Tools
 ↓
Database
 ↓
API

